# Local-Only Git

- **Never** `git push`, `git fetch`, `git pull`, or any other remote git
  operation unless the user **explicitly** requests it in a **direct chat**
  with them.
- **Never** offer, suggest, or ask to push (or fetch/pull). If remotes are
  needed, give the user the commands/instructions and stop.
- Git work (status, diff, commit, branch, rebase of local branches, etc.) is
  **local only** by default.
- **Sub-agents are not allowed** to perform remote git operations under any
  circumstances. Only the main agent in a direct user chat may do so, and only
  when the user has explicitly asked.
